  "body": "This PR adds methods swtich between use of LDO/DCDC (AKA SIMO) mode for the LR2021, it ports the workaround code mentioned in the datasheet:\r\n<img width=\"851\" height=\"952\" alt=\"SIMO-datasheet\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d00b916-f1ac-4a68-939a-691f44e577cb\" />\r\n\r\nRetrieved from: [Lora-net](https://github.com/Lora-net/usp/blob/main/smtc_rac_lib/radio_drivers/lr20xx_driver/src/lr20xx_workarounds.c)\r\n\r\n\r\n**Changes**\r\n\r\nThe two new functions mostly map:\r\n\r\n- `setDCDCworkaround `is `lr20xx_workarounds_dcdc_configure`\r\n- `resetDCDCworkaround `is `lr20xx_workarounds_dcdc_reset`\r\n\r\nI replaced the two register reads for frequency and is-high-freq with local vars and effectively inlined the 'lr20xx_workaround_dcdc_set_frequency' function.\r\n\r\nI have this running for on 3 LR2021's (LF), and the current consumption drops ~4ma for me. Back to back programming and checking the noise floor suggests you get a bit less than a dB lower on the noise floor with this workaround than without.\r\n\r\nI will do some more testing around this to make sure, I figured it's probably a good time for a review though.\r\n\r\nThe fix is applied for these functions (mentioned in datasheet, and code):\r\n\r\n- `setGfskModulationParams`\r\n- `setFlrcModulationParams`\r\n- `setLoRaModulationParams`\r\n- `setOokModulationParams`\r\n- `setRxPath`\r\n\r\nAnd also the undocumented reset called in that [code base](https://github.com/Lora-net/usp/blob/main/smtc_rac_lib/radio_drivers/lr20xx_driver/src/lr20xx_radio_common.c) on method:\r\n\r\n- `setPacketType`\r\n\r\nOne semi-related change to highlight:\r\n\r\n**setRegMode**\r\nI could not find info in the datasheet for a variant that takes ramp times as a parameter, so I've replaced the existing (unused) implementation. I can revert if you have more knowledge about this?\r\n\r\nQuite happy to make changes or answer questions :)",
